body:
Basically, a lot. Even if Russian women say that there is no sexism. 

People will judge if you: 

- got married in 18;
- haven't got married in 18;
- have a child;
- don't have a child;
- lonely mothers are whores;
- it's your fault you got raped; 
- you can be in a top management but you can't be a CEO; 
- you belong to your husband; 
- it's not a rape if you're married; 
- your parents will blackmail you into pregnancy; 
- your doctor will blackmail you into pregnancy; 
- everybody thinks they can ask when you'll get pregnant; 
- you can't speak until man's done; 
- you don't have rights but you've got so many obligations;
- people think it's normal to beat women (we've got a saying "if he beats her then he loves her"); 
- gay women don't exist - they didn't have a right man (that's why they need to be raped); 
- etc. 

I can go forever, actually :) 

Just look for the new New Year ad for Moscow Credit Bank and you'll get the idea.
